        <register>
          <name>ARB_R_CTRL0</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001000</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>The read arbitration control0</description>
          <resetValue>0x55555555</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>HPERI_TO_SPIC_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: WIFI/AES_SHA/OTPC/SIC
0x1: GDMA
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
[2]: slot 2 of arbiter
[3]: slot 3 of arbiter
[4]: slot 4 of arbiter
[5]: slot 5 of arbiter
[6]: slot 6 of arbiter
[7]: slot 7 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[31:24]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CPU_TO_SRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: KM4TZ
0x1: KM4NS
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
[2]: slot 2 of arbiter
[3]: slot 3 of arbiter
[4]: slot 4 of arbiter
[5]: slot 5 of arbiter
[6]: slot 6 of arbiter
[7]: slot 7 of arbiter</description>
              <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CPU_TO_PSRAM_ARB</name>
              <description>Read arbitration control register. Each slot should be set by a port number. The port number represents a master group.The master group is shown as following:
0x0: KM4TZ
0x1: KM4NS
And the following shows bit field of each slots:
[0]: slot 0 of arbiter
[1]: slot 1 of arbiter
