If byte_swap = 1,r data = {cpu_dataout_3, cpu_dataout_2, cpu_dataout_1, cpu_dataout_0}
Note that when user starts to read output data, 128bits (4 words) should be read together, that is, user is not allowed to read-write interleave. In other word, no partial read (3 words/2 words/1 words) is allowed, and no write can be inserted between reads.</description>
              <bitRange>[31:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>cpu_dataout_1</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000018</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description>CPU Data Output register 1</description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>cpu_dataout_1</name>
              <description>Output register bit[32*1+31:32*1] of the AES engine in the slave mode, only used in Slave_mode.
By waiting for the interrupt or polling the aes_slave_done signal to know whether the AES operation is completed. The result of AES will be stored in this register. The data order depends on chnx_aes_reg.config.byte_swap bit.
