        </register>
        <register>
          <name>ETHER_IO_CMD</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001434</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>max_dma_sel_0</name>
              <description>Select the dma burst size on bus(memory controller should assert continuous btrdy). 
00:16 DW(1DW=4B) 
01:32 DW 10:64 DW 11:128DW. 
AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support DMA burst length = 16DW</description>
              <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ShortDesFormat</name>
              <description>Short descriptor format. Set 1 tx/rx descriptor will use old format  - 4x32bit each item, set 0 use new format to support sram mapping AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support old format (1b'1)</description>
              <bitRange>[30:30]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>max_dma_sel_1</name>
              <description>see Ethernet_IO_CMD.bit31 AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support DMA burst length = 16DW</description>
              <bitRange>[29:29]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>en_early_tx</name>
              <description>default 0, 
0: disable, 
1: enable.  
Disable early tx by GAMC while tx command descriptor.IPCS, UDPCS or TCPCS are set to high. For multiple tx descriptor application, this field should be 0. For low lxbus throughput environment, this field should be 0. For slow clk_gmac application, this field should be 0.</description>
              <bitRange>[28:28]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TXPktTimer</name>
              <description>Timer to trigger TxOK interrupt before receipt of TxIntMitigation pkts. 0000 - no timer set 0001 ~ 1111 : the timer interval defining a multiple of TU  ex:  0011 = timer interval set to 3 x4 =12TU  Once TxOK is asserted the timer  mechanism is reinitialized.</description>
              <bitRange>[27:24]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxIntMitigation_3</name>
              <description>see Ethernet_IO_CMD.bit18-16</description>
              <bitRange>[23:23]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXPktTimer_3</name>
              <description>see Ethernet_IO_CMD.bit15-13</description>
              <bitRange>[22:22]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RxIntMitigation_3</name>
              <description>see Ethernet_IO_CMD.bit10-8</description>
              <bitRange>[21:21]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>tsh</name>
              <description>Tx Threshold: Specifies the threshold level in the Tx FIFO to begin the transmission. When the byte count of the data in the Tx FIFO reaches this level, (or the FIFO contains at least one complete packet or the end of a packet) the Ethernet module will transmit this packet. 
00:128B. 
01:256B. 
10:512B. 
11:1024B.    
For poor lxbus bandwidth, tsh should be set b11.      
In rle0516, this field should be setted 0 or 1 (128B).</description>
              <bitRange>[20:19]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxIntMitigation_2_0</name>
              <description>This sets the number of packets received before TxOK interrupt is triggered. 
0000- 1  pkt 
0001- 4  pkts 
0010- 8  pkts 
0011- 12 pkts 
0100- 16 pkts 
0101- 20 pkts 
0110- 24 pkts 
0111- 28 pkts ...</description>
              <bitRange>[18:16]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXPktTimer_2_0</name>
              <description>Timer to trigger RxOK interrupt before receipt of RxIntMitigation pkts. 
0000 - no timer set 
0001 ~ 1111 : the timer interval defining a multiple of TU  ex:  011 = timer interval set to 3 x4 =12TU  This only applies to packets of size larger than 128 bytes.  
Once RxOK is asserted the timer  mechanism is reinitialized.  For ingress pkt which is short than 128B, RxOK interrupt asserts after DMA completes.</description>
              <bitRange>[15:13]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXFTH</name>
              <description>Rx Threshold: Specifies the threshold level in the Rx FIFO to begin the transmission. When the byte count of the data in the Rx FIFO reaches this level, (or the FIFO contains at least one complete packet or the end of a packet) the Ethernet module will transmit this packet. 
00: 1024B 
01: 128B 
10: 256B 
11: 512B 
The rx threshold should be larger than maximum dma burst size. The combination of max_dma_sel and rxfth are listed as followed:
max_dma_sel            rxfth                                                                                       
b00(64B)               b00(1024B), b01 (128B), b10(256B), b11(512B).                                               
b01(128B)              b00(1024B), b10(256B), b11(512B).                                                           
b10(256B)              b00(1024B), b11(512B),
                                                                   
In rle0516:  SW should not set rxfth to 0b00 due to the rx fifo size is only 512B. The recommend value of rle0516 is 0b11 for performance concerns.  00 = no rx threshold. The Ethernet Module begins the transfer of data after having received a whole packet in the FIFO. 
01 = 32 bytes 
10 = 64 bytes 
11 = 128 bytes  
max_dma_sel            rxfth                                     
b0(64B)                b10(64B), b11(128B).                      
b1(128B)               b11(128B).</description>
              <bitRange>[12:11]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RxIntMitigation_2_0</name>
              <description>This sets the number of packets received before RxOK interrupt is triggered. 
0000- 1 pkt 
0001- 4 pkts 
0010- 8 pkts 
0011- 12pkts 
0100- 16 pkts 
0101- 20 pkts 
0110- 24 pkts 
0111- 28 pkts ...</description>
              <bitRange>[10:8]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>reg_int_timer_sel</name>
              <description>RXPktTimer, TXPktTimer Unit. (TU)  
       speed      TU              
00:      10M      25.6uS
00:      100M      2.56uS
00:      1000M      256nS
01:      10M      102.4uS
01:      100M      10.24uS
01:      1000M      1.024uS
10:      10M      409.6uS
10:      100M      40.96uS
10:      1000M      4.096uS
11:      10M      1.6mS
11:      100M      0.16mS
11:      1000M      16uS</description>
              <bitRange>[7:6]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RE</name>
              <description>MII Rx Enable</description>
              <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TE</name>
              <description>MII Tx Enable</description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxFN4th</name>
              <description>4th Priority DMA-Ethernet Transmit enable. 1: Enable.  0: Disable.</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxFN3rd</name>
              <description>3rd Priority DMA-Ethernet Transmit enable. 1: Enable. 0: Disable.</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxFN2nd</name>
              <description>2nd Priority DMA-Ethernet Transmit enable. 1: Enable. 0: Disable.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxFN1st</name>
              <description>1st Priority DMA-Ethernet Transmit enable. 1: Enable. 0: Disable.</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>IO_CMD1</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00001438</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0xB5000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>cf_orgcol_sel</name>
              <description>0: using GMAC internal generated collision signal 
1: using MII interface collision signal( (default 1: AmebaPro2)</description>
              <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Dsc_format_extra</name>
              <description>Extra descriptor format. In rle0437, bit28 is is write only. SW should set this field before set IO_CMD.TE or RE to 1. AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro
2 only support the fixed value 3b'011</description>
              <bitRange>[30:28]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>en_precise_dma</name>
              <description>0: disable precise DMA transfer. 
1: enable precise DMA transfer. 
AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support 1b'0 (disable precise DMA transfer)</description>
              <bitRange>[27:27]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Rxokint_msk_128B</name>
              <description>1: For ingress pkt which is short than 128B, RxOK interrupt asserts after DMA completes    (compatible issue). 0: For ingress pkt which is short than 128B, RxOK interrupt does not assert after DMA completes.</description>
              <bitRange>[26:26]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EN_RX_MRING</name>
              <description>Enable rx multiple rings. 
1: rx using multiple rings.    max: 6rings (ring1 to ring6). 
0 rx using single ring (ring1 only).  
SW should set this field before set IO_CMD.TE or RE to 1 AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support single rx ring</description>
              <bitRange>[25:25]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>EN_4GB</name>
              <description>1: support 4GB addressing in lx master bus.    For gmac used in rl0371 and after. 
0: no support. For project used in rle0390 and before.  
SW should set this field before set IO_CMD.TE or RE to 1 AmebaPro2 support 4GB addressing AmebaI/AmebaPro only support 1GB addressing</description>
              <bitRange>[24:24]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING6</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring6 enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
If RXRING6 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP6_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[21:21]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING5</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring5 enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
If RXRING5 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP5_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[20:20]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING4</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring4 enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
If RXRING4 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP4_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[19:19]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING3</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring3 enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
If RXRING3 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP3_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[18:18]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING2</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring2 enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
If RXRING2 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP2_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[17:17]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>RXRING1</name>
              <description>Ethernet-DMA Receive Ring1 enable. 
1: Enable. 
0: Disable. 
If RXRING1 is not used, SW should put one dummy rx command descriptor (own = 0) at RXFDP1_reg.</description>
              <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Tx_hl_pri_sel</name>
              <description>b00: TX ring uses strict priority. 
b01: TX ring uses high and low queue priority.    
Inside high queue, tx ring is round robin.    
Inside low queue, tx ring is round robin.   
Strict priority is used for high and low queue selection. b10 and b11: reserved.  In RL6266, when tx_hl_pri is 1, txq1_h and txq2_h are 1 and txq3_h, txq4_h and txq5_h are 0.  
SW should set this field before set IO_CMD.TE to 1. 
AmebaI/AmebaPro/AmebaPro2 only support the fixed value 2b'00</description>
              <bitRange>[15:14]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>TxFN5th</name>
              <description>5th Priority DMA-Ethernet Transmit enable. 
1: Enable.  
0: Disable. 
After IO_CMD.TE is set high, TxFN5th is writable.</description>
              <bitRange>[8:8]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>txq5_h</name>
              <description>1: TxFN5th is a high queue. 
0: TxFN5th is a low queue. 
This field is only used in eee.</description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>txq4_h</name>
              <description>1: TxFN4th is a high queue. 
0: TxFN4th is a low queue. 
This field is only used in eee.</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>txq3_h</name>
              <description>1: TxFN3rd is a high queue. 
0: TxFN3rd is a low queue. 
This field is only used in eee.</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>txq2_h</name>
              <description>1: TxFN2nd is a high queue. 
0: TxFN2nd is a low queue. 
This field is only used in eee.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>txq1_h</name>
              <description>1: TxFN1st is a high queue. 
0: TxFN1st is a low queue. 
This field is only used in eee.</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>WOL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000143C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>wol_imr</name>
              <description>Interrupt mask of wol_pme.</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Wol_pme</name>
              <description>HW asserts pme when  
a.HW entered wol idle state and  
b.received magic ingress pkt. 
HW asserts pme to wake up system.  
Wol_pme indicates: 
0: No magic pkt receives. 
1: HW had received one magic pkt and system should wake up.</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Wol_sts</name>
              <description>HW enters wol idle state when  
a. SW issues wol_cmd state and  
b. HW tx/rx function enter idle state.  
Wol_sts indicates: 
0: HW is not in wol idle state. 
1: HW is in wol idle state.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>Wol_cmd</name>
              <description>Issue wol command by SW</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
      </registers>
    </peripheral>
    <peripheral>
      <name>DVP_REG</name>
      <baseAddress>0x41805000</baseAddress>
      <size>0x00000084</size>
      <addressBlock>
        <offset>0x00000000</offset>
        <size>0x00000084</size>
        <usage>registers</usage>
      </addressBlock>
      <registers>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_TRANSFER</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000000</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>dvp_state</name>
              <description>1: dvp enable
0: dvp disable</description>
              <bitRange>[8:8]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>dvp_start</name>
              <description>Start The transfer is launch if set this bit. When clear this bit, hardware will stop transfer after current image frame finish transfer.
Dvp_start置1表示开流
停流方式可以选择配置immediate_stop或者是frame_stop来实现立即停流或者帧后停流.配置完immediate_stop或者是frame_stop后,dvp_state会自动拉低,拉低时间参考immediate_stop或者是frame_stop寄存器描述</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_CONFIG</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000004</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>pclk_stop_mode</name>
              <description>PCLK Stop mode. 
Used when sensor uses HSYNC/VSYNC to perform gating on pclk, or pclk_stop_en open
0: normal
1: sensor pixclk stop mode</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>pixclk_edge_sel</name>
              <description>Pixel clock sample edge. 0: falling edge, 1: rising edge.</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>vsync_polarity</name>
              <description>Vsync polarity 0: active low, 1: active high.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>hsync_polarity</name>
              <description>Hsync polarity 0: active low, 1: active high.</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_CROP_START_X</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000000C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>dmy_pix_num</name>
              <description>YUV path Unit: Bytes.
This field indicates the number of dummy data before the valid data output. Hardware must bypass these dummy data and not sample the dummy data.
yuv422 format config value is a multiple of 4

Eg: For YUV422 format, each pixel is represented by 2 bytes. Therefore, setting this field to 8 means skipping 4 pixels

In formats like YUYV, YVYU, UYVY, and VYUY, data streams from the sensor to the DVP with each two pixels sharing the same UV components. Since each pair requires 2 pixels of 16bpp, it amounts to a total of 4 bytes. Therefore, operations involving this data should be done in multiples of 4 bytes.
用于crop丢掉数据</description>
              <bitRange>[12:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_CROP_START_Y</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000010</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>dmy_line_num</name>
              <description>YUV path
This field indicates the number of dummy line before the valid line output. Hardware must bypass these dummy lines and not sample the dummy line data.
用于crop丢掉数据</description>
              <bitRange>[11:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_WIDTH</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000014</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>pix_num_pre</name>
              <description>YUV path Unit:bytes
HORIZON_NUM10:0. This field indicates the number of valid data per line.
yuv422 format config value is a multiple of 4

Eg: For YUV422 format, each pixel is represented by 2 bytes. Therefore, setting this field to 8 means reserved 4 pixels
用于crop选取有效数据,选取后的数据送往sub sample</description>
              <bitRange>[12:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_HEIGHT</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000018</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>line_num_pre</name>
              <description>YUV path
VERTICAL_NUM10:0. This field indicates the number of valid line per frame.
用于crop选取有效数据,选取后的数据送往sub sample</description>
              <bitRange>[11:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_FRAME_CNT</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000001C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>frame_num</name>
              <description>Frame_cnt 7:0. This field is used to count the number of active Vsync from RealTimeImage transfer start. If the RealTimeImage transfer stop, the value of this register do not change. As soon as trigger RealTimeImage transfer, reset the value of thi register and restart to count.</description>
              <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_SUBSAMPLE_CTL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000020</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>l_sub_sample_en</name>
              <description>YUV path
Vertical (Line) Sub Sample control. 
0: not sub sample, 1: sub sample.</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>p_sub_sample_en</name>
              <description>YUV path
Horizontal (Pixel) Sub sample control.
0: not sub sample, 1: sub sample.</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_SUBSAMPLE_CFG</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000024</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>l_sub_vld_num</name>
              <description>YUV path
Vertical Sub sample valid line number. 
1-15:有效的line num是1-15
0:有效的line num是16</description>
              <bitRange>[15:12]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>l_sub_drop_num</name>
              <description>YUV path
Vertical Sub sample invalid line number. 
1-15:丢掉的line num是1-15
0:丢掉的line num是16</description>
              <bitRange>[11:8]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>p_sub_vld_num</name>
              <description>YUV path
Horizontal (Pixel) Sub sample valid pixel number.
yuv422 format config value: 
4: vld 4 byte
8: vld 8 byte
12: vld 12 byte
0: vld 16 byte</description>
              <bitRange>[7:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>p_sub_drop_num</name>
              <description>YUV path
Horizontal (Line) Sub sample invalid pixel number. 
yuv422 format config value: 
4: drop 4 byte
8: drop 8 byte
12: drop 12 byte
0: drop 16 byte</description>
              <bitRange>[3:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_FRMAE_VLD_CTL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000028</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>frame_vld_num</name>
              <description>FRAME_VALID_NUM
4'b0: all frame are valid
otherwise: one frame valid in every (FRAME_VALID_NUM + 1 ) frames</description>
              <bitRange>[3:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_YUV_TRANSFER</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000002C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>image_format</name>
              <description>yuv422 sensor in format
2'b00: YUYV YUYV
2'b01: YVYU YVYU
2'b10: UYVY UYVY
2'b11: VYUY VYUY</description>
              <bitRange>[1:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_JPEG_TRANSFER</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000030</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>jpg_en</name>
              <description>DVP JPEG MODE EN
1: Enable DVP JPEG 
0: Disable DVP JPEG</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>jpg_mode</name>
              <description>DVP JPEG Mode
3'b000:Valid mode
Use VSYNC as the frame synchronization signal and HSYNC as the horizontal synchronization signal. There is no dummy data in the frame. Support VSYNC pulse or level timing
3'b001:Frame mode
Use VSYNC as the frame synchronization signal and HSYNC as the horizontal synchronization signal. There is dummy data in the frame. The frame contains valid data length , and valid data length is at the beginning of each line.
3'b010:Frame mode
Use VSYNC as the frame synchronization signal and HSYNC as the horizontal synchronization signal. There is dummy data in the frame. The frame contains valid data length , and valid data length is at the end of each line.
3'b011:Frame mode
Use VSYNC as the frame synchronization signal and HSYNC as the horizontal synchronization signal. There is dummy data in the frame. The frame does not contains valid data length.
3'b100:Use HSYNC as the frame synchronization signal,no dummy data</description>
              <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_PCLK_GATING_CTL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000034</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>pclk_gating_en</name>
              <description>PCLK_GATING_EN
用于PCLK被VSYNC/HSYNC gating的情况,配合pclk_stop_mode使用,当pclk_gating_en置1时,pclk_stop_mode也要置1</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_PAD_CTL</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000038</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>pix_bit_swp</name>
              <description>pixel bit switch
2'b01:
pad[9:0]={bit7,bit6,bit5,bit4,bit3,bit2,bit1,bit0,2'd0}
2'b10:
pad[9:0]={2'd0,bit0,bit1,bit2,bit3,bit4,bit5,bit6,bit7}
2'b00&amp;2'b11:
pad[9:0]={2'd0,bit7,bit6,bit5,bit4,bit3,bit2,bit1,bit0}
YUV422 &amp; JPG stream only 1 byte data valid in one PCLK cycle</description>
              <bitRange>[1:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_STOP</name>
          <addressOffset>0x0000003C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>frame_stop</name>
              <description>The stop will not be triggered untill the current frame ends
当前帧结束以后停流(帧已经发送到psram中),下一帧不接收,当前帧结束以后会拉低dvp_state</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>immediate_stop</name>
              <description>If set this bit, hardware will stop transfer and return idle state immediately. Hardware will auto clear this bit.
立即停流,同时拉低dvp_state.dma里存储的outstanding data依旧会发送出来,防止卡死platform</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>write-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_JPG_FRAME_LENGTH</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000040</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>jpg_frame_length</name>
              <description>jpg frame size</description>
              <bitRange>[21:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_INT_ST</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000044</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>frame_cnt_int</name>
              <description>all frame buffer are fulled frames , and DVP will not to receive frames in time.then gen overflow int, need to check and clear frame status done register</description>
              <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ddr_overflow_int</name>
              <description>ddr_overflow_int
Only for frame buffer mode
The allocated psram/ddr capacith is less than one frame</description>
              <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>buf_overflow_int</name>
              <description>dma buffer overflow int
DMA needs to cache a certain amount of data before sending data to psram/ddr. The cached data is placed in buffer(memory), If there is too much cache and it is not sent, it means overflow</description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_break_int</name>
              <description>frame_break_int
yuv422 mode, The pixel count is internally compared with the configured frame size(ddr_len)
pixel count是经过sub sample后的数据进行计算,这时的数据会送入缓存的buffer,等待传入psram.
pixel count会与ddr_len进行比对,当pixel count小于ddr_len时会触发中断.
情况1:ddr len等于frame size, 当前帧破图,需要丢掉
情况2:ddr_len大于frame size,该中断没有参考意义
情况3: ddr_len小于frame size,可以通过ddr_overflow_int得知信息,需要及时调整ddr_len,使其满足frame_size
jpg mode, The pixel will be counted internally, and for jpg timing with valid data length, it will be compared with the data length</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_start_int</name>
              <description>frame_start_int
indicating that DVP is receiving a frame of image from sensor
both yuv fb and jpeg
帧开始中断,这时dma已经准备发送图片</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_end_int</name>
              <description>frame_end_int
both yuv fb and jpeg
indicating that DVP has transfered one frame of image to memory</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>line_end_int</name>
              <description>line_end_int
Only for YUV path
indicates that the image has been transferred to the configured number of lines(interrupt_line_num).
计算的是dma向psram中传输的line num</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>DVP_INT_RAW</name>
          <addressOffset>0x00000048</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <description></description>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>frame_cnt_raw_int</name>
              <description>frame buffer cnt overflow raw int, need to clear frame status done</description>
              <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ddr_overflow_raw_int</name>
              <description>ddr_overflow_raw_int
ddr/psram中断,通过所配置的ddr_len进行判断,模块内部会对传输的burst_length进行计数,当计数大于ddr_len时会触发中断</description>
              <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>buf_overflow_raw_int</name>
              <description>buf_overflow_raw_int
dma缓存buffer中断,dma会缓存发往ddr/psram的数据,当满足一笔burst时dma会发起请求.当请求一直得不到回应同时缓存buffer溢出时会触发中断.</description>
              <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_break_raw_int</name>
              <description>frame_break_raw_int</description>
              <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_start_raw_int</name>
              <description>frame_start_raw_int</description>
              <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>frame_end_raw_int</name>
              <description>frame_end_raw_int</description>
              <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>line_end_raw_int</name>
              <description>line_end_raw_int</description>
              <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
